  "body": "## Summary\n- Treat non-empty local round-cache files as valid without probing the NAS\n- Only touch the source path when the local cache entry is missing or empty\n- Update the overlay status text to describe cache checking instead of copying\n\n## Feature Contracts\n- Affected contract: `docs/feature-contracts/desktop-status.md`\n- The `file_sync` shape and steady-state invariant are preserved: a healthy already-cached round still reports `cached == round.length`, `copied == 0`, `missing == 0`, and `failed == 0`.\n- The round-and-advance behavior is unchanged; the whole current round is still cached before playback.\n\n## Tests\n- `cargo test -p shows-core`\n- Manual release smoke: replaced `D:\\Downloads\\shows\\shows-desktop.exe`; timed restart reached `49 cached`, `0 copied`, `0 missing`, `0 failed` in about 1.47s.",
